pg?sqp=-oaymwE9CNACELwBSFryq4qpAy8IARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAHwAQH4Af4JgALQBYoCDAgAEAEYYSBlKFAwDw==&rs=AOn4CLDzc4BKVN-44GieOUmS2RUD8pcBvw", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "36", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCOADEOgC8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-CYAC0AWKAgwIABABGGEgZShQMA8=&rs=AOn4CLDnRcAEzV4bJzpGlCFQJ9eEkpecIw", "height": 360, "width": 480, "preference": -7, "id": "37", "resolution": "480x360"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/Meue08LjBwc/hqdefault.webp", "preference": -6, "id": "38"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/sddefault.jpg", "preference": -5, "id": "39"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/sddefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAFEOAD8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-CYAC0AWKAgwIABABGGEgZShQMA8=&rs=AOn4CLCyMyONLSqsUcmoKXOxFbPpEApDgQ", "height": 480, "width": 640, "preference": -5, "id": "40", "resolution": "640x480"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/Meue08LjBwc/sddefault.webp", "preference": -4, "id": "41"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/hq720.jpg", "preference": -3, "id": "42"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/Meue08LjBwc/hq720.webp", "preference": -2, "id": "43"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/maxresdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAKENAF8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-CYAC0AWKAgwIABABGGEgZShQMA8=&rs=AOn4CLCutQry_-J_fHqfAzGUX3OAqeVN3A", "preference": -1, "id": "44"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/maxresdefault.jpg", "height": 1080, "width": 1920, "preference": -1, "id": "45", "resolution": "1920x1080"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/Meue08LjBwc/maxresdefault.webp", "preference": 0, "id": "46"}], "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Meue08LjBwc/maxresdefault.jpg", "description": "Hi!\nWhile traveling to Sundarban, I tried to collect few snaps, videos  (Feb 2022). Thanks to Shihab Uddin (https://www.facebook.com/suahmed03) to make this arrangement smoothly. We reserved a small private ship for 10 people and stayed 3 days - 2 nights. Foods were delicious (3 meals including snacks) and we enjoyed the amazing natural beauties. \nThe Sundarbans mangrove forest, one of the largest such forests in the world (140,000 ha), lies on the delta of the Ganges, Brahmaputra and Meghna rivers on the Bay of Bengal. It is adjacent to the border of India’s Sundarbans World Heritage site inscribed in 1987. The site is intersected by a complex network of tidal waterways, mudflats and small islands of salt-tolerant mangrove forests, and presents an excellent example of ongoing ecological processes. The area is known for its wide range of fauna, including 260 bird species, the Bengal tiger and other threatened species such as the estuarine crocodile and the Indian python (Data collected from Internet).\nTravelling to Sundarban is quite safe and you will get trained guide and gunman. So, I hope everyone should take this opportunity to visit Sundarban :). Cause, as I booked everything from abroad, felt bit insecure but everything went well. From my personal view, you have to enjoy nature during this timing, otherwise, it will be bit boring for anyone. \nThanks for watching and the last paragraph (bengali written) is about the advertisement from the tour group. \n\n#sundarban #sundarbanvlogs #sundarbanforest #bangladesh #bangladeshivlog #mangrove #mangroveforest #tiger #khulna #khulna_city #bagerhat #dimerchor #koromjol #Jamtolaseabeach #kochikhali #travelvlog #travelguide #natural #naturalbeauty #bayofbengal #worldheritage \n\nবাংলাদেশের একমাত্র সুন্দরবনেই নৌযানে করে তিনদিন ভ্রমনের সুযোগ পাচ্ছেন।\nসুন্দরবনের প্রকৃতির উপভোগের সাথে সাথে খুব কাছে থেকে বন্যপ্রানী দেখার এক অপূর্ব সুযোগ পাওয়া যাবে। এমন কি ভাগ্য ভালো হলে এই সময় পৃথিবী বিখ্যাত রয়েল বেঙ্গল টাইগারের দেখা মিলতে পারে। এই সময় সমুদ্রকে পাবেন আপনার মনের মত করে। \n\nআমাদের ভ্রমনের স্থানঃ \n- হারবাড়িয়া\n- কটকা অফিস \n- ওয়াচ টাওয়ার\n- জামতলা সী বিচ\n- ডিমের চর\n- কচিখালি\n- করমজল", "channel_id": "UCWeqwKG9OkVM9QM87s6fYVw", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCWeqwKG9OkVM9QM87s